      "equations": [
        {
          "_comment": "TFG-1a and TFG-1d coincide here only because one formulation at share 1 makes the average ethanol volume equal the formulation's own. On a two-formulation supply they would differ, and the assertion below would not move.",
          "lhs": "tfgKGasoline",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "apply_expression_template",
            "args": [],
            "name": "tank_fuel_k_gasoline",
            "bindings": {
              "etoh_volume": "tfgEtohVolume"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "tfgKEthanol",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "apply_expression_template",
            "args": [],
            "name": "tank_fuel_k_ethanol",
            "bindings": {
              "etoh_volume": "tfgEtohVolume"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "tfgGasPortionRVP",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "apply_expression_template",
            "args": [],
            "name": "tank_fuel_gas_portion_rvp",
            "bindings": {
              "rvp": "tfgFormulationRVP",
              "etoh_volume": "tfgEtohVolume",
              "k_gasoline": "tfgKGasoline",
              "k_ethanol": "tfgKEthanol"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "tfgGasPortionRVPE85",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "apply_expression_template",
            "args": [],
            "name": "tank_fuel_gas_portion_rvp",
            "bindings": {
              "rvp": "tfgFormulationRVPE85",
              "etoh_volume": "tfgEtohVolume",
              "k_gasoline": "tfgKGasoline",
              "k_ethanol": "tfgKEthanol"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "_comment": "TFG-1b's denominator: the share sum over EVERY surviving row, including rows whose numerator operand is NULL. One row here.",
          "lhs": "tfgShareSum",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "*",
            "args": [
              "tfgMarketShare",
              "tfgYearMultiplicity"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "tfgLinearAverageRVP",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "/",
            "args": [
              {
                "op": "*",
                "args": [
                  "tfgFormulationRVP",
                  "tfgMarketShare",
                  "tfgYearMultiplicity"
                ]
              },
              "tfgShareSum"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "tfgAverageEtohVolume",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "/",
            "args": [
              {
                "op": "*",
                "args": [
                  "tfgEtohVolume",
                  "tfgMarketShare",
                  "tfgYearMultiplicity"
                ]
              },
              "tfgShareSum"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "tfgAverageGasPortionRVP",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "/",
            "args": [
              {
                "op": "*",
                "args": [
                  "tfgGasPortionRVP",
                  "tfgMarketShare",
                  "tfgYearMultiplicity"
                ]
              },
              "tfgShareSum"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "_comment": "TFG-1e. Recombining the portion tfgGasPortionRVP stripped out must return the formulation's own RVP; the assertion checks exactly that round trip, which is what makes TFG-3b's ratio meaningful.",
          "lhs": "tfgNoWeatheringReddyRVP",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "apply_expression_template",
            "args": [],
            "name": "tank_fuel_reddy_rvp",
            "bindings": {
              "etoh_volume": "tfgAverageEtohVolume",
              "gas_portion_rvp": "tfgAverageGasPortionRVP",
              "k_gasoline": "tfgKGasoline",
              "k_ethanol": "tfgKEthanol"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "tfgCommingledRVP",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "*",
            "args": [
              "tfgLinearAverageRVP",
              "tfgCommingleFactor"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "tfgZoneEvapTemp",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "apply_expression_template",
            "args": [],
            "name": "tank_fuel_zone_evap_temp",
            "bindings": {
              "min_temperature": "tfgZoneMinTemperature",
              "max_temperature": "tfgZoneMaxTemperature"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "_comment": "The SAME expression as tank_fuel_rvp_loss_ratio WITHOUT its max(0, .). Carried only so the clamp has a negative control: if the two were equal the clamp would be untested, and on this fixture the clamp is the one part of TFG that is load-bearing (docs/evap-fvv.md 2.5).",
          "lhs": "tfgRVPLossRatioUnclamped",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "/",
            "args": [
              {
                "op": "+",
                "args": [
                  -2.4908,
                  {
                    "op": "*",
                    "args": [
                      0.026196,
                      "tfgZoneEvapTemp"
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "op": "*",
                    "args": [
                      0.00076898,
                      "tfgZoneEvapTemp",
                      "tfgAverageGasPortionRVP"
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "op": "+",
                "args": [
                  -0.086,
                  {
                    "op": "*",
                    "args": [
                      0.070592,
                      "tfgAverageGasPortionRVP"
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "tfgRVPLossRatio",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "apply_expression_template",
            "args": [],
            "name": "tank_fuel_rvp_loss_ratio",
            "bindings": {
              "zone_evap_temp": "tfgZoneEvapTemp",
              "gas_portion_rvp": "tfgAverageGasPortionRVP"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "tfgWeatheredGasPortionRVP",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "*",
            "args": [
              "tfgAverageGasPortionRVP",
              {
                "op": "-",
                "args": [
                  1.0,
                  {
                    "op": "*",
                    "args": [
                      "tfgRVPLossRatio",
                      0.049
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "tfgWeatheredReddyRVP",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "apply_expression_template",
            "args": [],
            "name": "tank_fuel_reddy_rvp",
            "bindings": {
              "etoh_volume": "tfgAverageEtohVolume",
              "gas_portion_rvp": "tfgWeatheredGasPortionRVP",
              "k_gasoline": "tfgKGasoline",
              "k_ethanol": "tfgKEthanol"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "_comment": "TFG-3b. averageTankGasoline.RVP for fuel type 1. This is the number the whole component exists to produce: docs/evap-fvv.md 0.3 measures that perturbing it by +2 moves the fixture's total from 558.97 g to 612.56 g, while perturbing anything in the venting chain moves nothing at all.",
          "lhs": "tfgRVP",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "/",
            "args": [
              {
                "op": "*",
                "args": [
                  "tfgWeatheredReddyRVP",
                  "tfgCommingledRVP"
                ]
              },
              "tfgNoWeatheringReddyRVP"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "tfgAverageGasPortionRVPE85",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "/",
            "args": [
              {
                "op": "*",
                "args": [
                  "tfgGasPortionRVPE85",
                  "tfgMarketShare",
                  "tfgYearMultiplicity"
                ]
              },
              "tfgShareSum"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "tfgNoWeatheringReddyRVPE85",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "apply_expression_template",
            "args": [],
            "name": "tank_fuel_reddy_rvp",
            "bindings": {
              "etoh_volume": "tfgAverageEtohVolume",
              "gas_portion_rvp": "tfgAverageGasPortionRVPE85",
              "k_gasoline": "tfgKGasoline",
              "k_ethanol": "tfgKEthanol"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "tfgRVPLossRatioE85",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "apply_expression_template",
            "args": [],
            "name": "tank_fuel_rvp_loss_ratio",
            "bindings": {
              "zone_evap_temp": "tfgZoneEvapTemp",
              "gas_portion_rvp": "tfgAverageGasPortionRVPE85"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "tfgWeatheredReddyRVPE85",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "apply_expression_template",
            "args": [],
            "name": "tank_fuel_reddy_rvp",
            "bindings": {
              "etoh_volume": "tfgAverageEtohVolume",
              "gas_portion_rvp": {
                "op": "*",
                "args": [
                  "tfgAverageGasPortionRVPE85",
                  {
                    "op": "-",
                    "args": [
                      1.0,
                      {
                        "op": "*",
                        "args": [
                          "tfgRVPLossRatioE85",
                          0.049
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              "k_gasoline": "tfgKGasoline",
              "k_ethanol": "tfgKEthanol"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "tfgRVPE85",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "/",
            "args": [
              {
                "op": "*",
                "args": [
                  "tfgWeatheredReddyRVPE85",
                  {
                    "op": "*",
                    "args": [
                      "tfgFormulationRVPE85",
                      "tfgCommingleFactor"
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              "tfgNoWeatheringReddyRVPE85"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "_comment": "TVV-8 floors the temperature at 40 degF for the tempAdjustment polynomial but NOT for the rvpAdjustment one, which instead takes the value 1 below 40. Two different treatments of the same threshold, and this fixture is at 59.5 degF so it exercises neither guard.",
          "lhs": "adjTempFloored",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "max",
            "args": [
              "adjTemperature",
              40.0
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "adjTempAdjustment",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "apply_expression_template",
            "args": [],
            "name": "cubic_in",
            "bindings": {
              "term3": "etaTerm3",
              "term2": "etaTerm2",
              "term1": "etaTerm1",
              "constant": "etaConstant",
              "x": "adjTempFloored"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "adjRvpTerm0",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "apply_expression_template",
            "args": [],
            "name": "knot_interpolate",
            "bindings": {
              "low_value": "knotLowTerm3",
              "high_value": "knotHighTerm3",
              "low_knot": "knotLowRVP",
              "high_knot": "knotHighRVP",
              "x": "tfgRVP"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "adjRvpTerm1",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "apply_expression_template",
            "args": [],
            "name": "knot_interpolate",
            "bindings": {
              "low_value": "knotLowTerm2",
              "high_value": "knotHighTerm2",
              "low_knot": "knotLowRVP",
              "high_knot": "knotHighRVP",
              "x": "tfgRVP"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "adjRvpTerm2",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "apply_expression_template",
            "args": [],
            "name": "knot_interpolate",
            "bindings": {
              "low_value": "knotLowTerm1",
              "high_value": "knotHighTerm1",
              "low_knot": "knotLowRVP",
              "high_knot": "knotHighRVP",
              "x": "tfgRVP"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "adjRvpTerm3",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "apply_expression_template",
            "args": [],
            "name": "knot_interpolate",
            "bindings": {
              "low_value": "knotLowConstant",
              "high_value": "knotHighConstant",
              "low_knot": "knotLowRVP",
              "high_knot": "knotHighRVP",
              "x": "tfgRVP"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "_comment": "The SECOND call site of cubic_in, with different coefficients and a different argument. That there are two is what makes cubic_in a template rather than an inlined polynomial.",
          "lhs": "adjRvpAdjustment",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "ifelse",
            "args": [
              {
                "op": ">=",
                "args": [
                  "adjTemperature",
                  40.0
                ]
              },
              {
                "op": "apply_expression_template",
                "args": [],
                "name": "cubic_in",
                "bindings": {
                  "term3": "adjRvpTerm0",
                  "term2": "adjRvpTerm1",
                  "term1": "adjRvpTerm2",
                  "constant": "adjRvpTerm3",
                  "x": "adjTemperature"
                }
              },
              1.0
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "_comment": "TVV-8's adjustment for operating mode 300, fuel type 1. docs/evap-fvv.md 7.2: dropping it -- which is what a port that skipped TankFuelGenerator gets -- lands the fixture 2.79 per cent high.",
          "lhs": "adjOperatingAdjustment",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "*",
            "args": [
              "adjTempAdjustment",
              "adjRvpAdjustment"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "adjE85RvpTerm0",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "apply_expression_template",
            "args": [],
            "name": "knot_interpolate",
            "bindings": {
              "low_value": "knotE85LowTerm3",
              "high_value": "knotLowTerm3",
              "low_knot": "knotE85LowRVP",
              "high_knot": "knotE85HighRVP",
              "x": "tfgRVPE85"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "adjE85RvpTerm1",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "apply_expression_template",
            "args": [],
            "name": "knot_interpolate",
            "bindings": {
              "low_value": "knotE85LowTerm2",
              "high_value": "knotLowTerm2",
              "low_knot": "knotE85LowRVP",
              "high_knot": "knotE85HighRVP",
              "x": "tfgRVPE85"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "adjE85RvpTerm2",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "apply_expression_template",
            "args": [],
            "name": "knot_interpolate",
            "bindings": {
              "low_value": "knotE85LowTerm1",
              "high_value": "knotLowTerm1",
              "low_knot": "knotE85LowRVP",
              "high_knot": "knotE85HighRVP",
              "x": "tfgRVPE85"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "adjE85RvpTerm3",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "apply_expression_template",
            "args": [],
            "name": "knot_interpolate",
            "bindings": {
              "low_value": "knotE85LowConstant",
              "high_value": "knotLowConstant",
              "low_knot": "knotE85LowRVP",
              "high_knot": "knotE85HighRVP",
              "x": "tfgRVPE85"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "adjE85RvpAdjustment",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "apply_expression_template",
            "args": [],
            "name": "cubic_in",
            "bindings": {
              "term3": "adjE85RvpTerm0",
              "term2": "adjE85RvpTerm1",
              "term1": "adjE85RvpTerm2",
              "constant": "adjE85RvpTerm3",
              "x": "adjTemperature"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "adjE85OperatingAdjustment",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "*",
            "args": [
              "adjTempAdjustment",
              "adjE85RvpAdjustment"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "tvvInnerT0",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "apply_expression_template",
            "args": [],
            "name": "tvv_quadratic_root",
            "bindings": {
              "canister_load": "tvvCanisterLoad",
              "a": "tvvT0a",
              "b1": "tvvT0b1",
              "b0": "tvvT0b0",
              "c2": "tvvT0c2",
              "c1": "tvvT0c1",
              "c0": "tvvT0c0"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "tvvInnerT2",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "apply_expression_template",
            "args": [],
            "name": "tvv_quadratic_root",
            "bindings": {
              "canister_load": "tvvCanisterLoad",
              "a": "tvvT2a",
              "b1": "tvvT2b1",
              "b0": "tvvT2b0",
              "c2": "tvvT2c2",
              "c1": "tvvT2c1",
              "c0": "tvvT2c0"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "_comment": "T0, T1 and T2 are the DEGENERATE weight = 1 case of the blend, which is why one template covers all six labels (docs/evap-fvv.md 2.10, Form 2).",
          "lhs": "tvvEquationT0",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "apply_expression_template",
            "args": [],
            "name": "tvv_blend",
            "bindings": {
              "inner_p": "tvvInnerT0",
              "inner_q": "tvvInnerT0",
              "weight": 1.0
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "tvvInnerT2Clamped",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "apply_expression_template",
            "args": [],
            "name": "tvv_quadratic_root",
            "bindings": {
              "canister_load": "tvvCanisterLoadClamped",
              "a": "tvvT2a",
              "b1": "tvvT2b1",
              "b0": "tvvT2b0",
              "c2": "tvvT2c2",
              "c1": "tvvT2c1",
              "c0": "tvvT2c0"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "tvvInnerT0Clamped",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "apply_expression_template",
            "args": [],
            "name": "tvv_quadratic_root",
            "bindings": {
              "canister_load": "tvvCanisterLoadClamped",
              "a": "tvvT0a",
              "b1": "tvvT0b1",
              "b0": "tvvT0b0",
              "c2": "tvvT0c2",
              "c1": "tvvT0c1",
              "c0": "tvvT0c0"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "tvvEquationT3",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "apply_expression_template",
            "args": [],
            "name": "tvv_blend",
            "bindings": {
              "inner_p": "tvvInnerT0",
              "inner_q": "tvvInnerT2",
              "weight": "tvvT3Weight"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "_comment": "The negative control for tvv_blend's clamp: the same expression at a load where both inner roots are negative. 0.8*(-0.4649) + 0.2*(-0.3816) is -0.4483, and the assertion expects 0.",
          "lhs": "tvvEquationT3Clamped",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "apply_expression_template",
            "args": [],
            "name": "tvv_blend",
            "bindings": {
              "inner_p": "tvvInnerT0Clamped",
              "inner_q": "tvvInnerT2Clamped",
              "weight": "tvvT3Weight"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "tvvLeakEquationL3",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "apply_expression_template",
            "args": [],
            "name": "tvv_leak_linear",
            "bindings": {
              "coefficient": "tvvL3Coefficient",
              "tvg_daily": "tvvTVGDaily"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "tvvCumulative",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "apply_expression_template",
            "args": [],
            "name": "tvv_cumulative_vented",
            "bindings": {
              "reg_class_fraction": "tvvRegClassFraction",
              "leak_fraction": "tvvLeakFraction",
              "tvv_equation": "tvvEquationT0",
              "leak_equation": "tvvLeakEquationL3"
            }
          }
        }
      ],
      "tests": [
        {
          "id": "tfg_strips_and_recombines_the_ethanol_term_exactly",
          "description": "TFG-1a's gasPortionRVP removes the ethanol contribution from a formulation's RVP and TFG-1e's Reddy recombination puts it back. tfgNoWeatheringReddyRVP must therefore return the formulation's own 8.0 psi EXACTLY, and 7.7 for E85. That round trip is the only thing making TFG-3b's final ratio (weathered Reddy x commingled / unweathered Reddy) a rescaling rather than a rescrambling. What breaks if this is wrong: kGasoline and kEthanol are evaluated at the AVERAGE ethanol volume in TFG-1d and at the FORMULATION's in TFG-1a; on this fixture the two coincide because there is one formulation at market share 1, so a port that used the wrong one would pass here and fail on any multi-formulation supply (docs/evap-fvv.md 8.1).",
          "time_span": {
            "start": 0.0,
            "end": 0.0
          },
          "assertions": [
            {
              "variable": "tfgKGasoline",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 1.0433
            },
            {
              "variable": "tfgKEthanol",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 6.66159041209328
            },
            {
              "variable": "tfgGasPortionRVP",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 6.888222419479373
            },
            {
              "variable": "tfgGasPortionRVPE85",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 6.568723393951401
            },
            {
              "variable": "tfgNoWeatheringReddyRVP",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 8.0
            },
            {
              "variable": "tfgNoWeatheringReddyRVPE85",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 7.7
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "tfg_weathering_is_clamped_off_and_the_clamp_is_what_decides_the_answer",
          "description": "TFG-2a puts zone 261610 at 78.344292 degF, and at that temperature TFG-2c's ratio is NEGATIVE (-0.058739) for both fuel types. tank_fuel_rvp_loss_ratio's max(0, .) is therefore the operative step: it turns -0.0587 into 0, the gasoline portion passes through unweathered, and averageTankGasoline.RVP comes out at exactly the supplied formulations' 8.0 and 7.7. tfgRVPLossRatioUnclamped is the same expression WITHOUT the clamp and is asserted at the negative value, so the clamp is checked from both sides rather than being an untested guard. What breaks if this is wrong: dropping the clamp weathers the RVP by 0.049 x -0.0587, RVP rises to about 8.02, and docs/evap-fvv.md 7.2 shows the fixture's total moves with it.",
          "time_span": {
            "start": 0.0,
            "end": 0.0
          },
          "assertions": [
            {
              "variable": "tfgZoneEvapTemp",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 78.34429184515731
            },
            {
              "variable": "tfgRVPLossRatioUnclamped",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": -0.05873938402269431
            },
            {
              "variable": "tfgRVPLossRatio",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 0.0
            },
            {
              "variable": "tfgWeatheredGasPortionRVP",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 6.888222419479373
            },
            {
              "variable": "tfgRVP",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 8.0
            },
            {
              "variable": "tfgRVPE85",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 7.700000000000001
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "tvv8_adjustment_is_two_cubics_and_the_second_needs_the_generated_rvp",
          "description": "TVV-8's operating-mode adjustment is evapTemperatureAdjustment's cubic in max(T, 40) TIMES the cubic whose coefficients are evapRVPTemperatureAdjustment's four terms interpolated at averageTankGasoline.RVP. At RVP 8.0 the interpolation sits exactly ON the RVP-8 knot, so adjRvpTerm0..3 reproduce that knot's terms unchanged -- which is the check that knot_interpolate's bracket selection picked the right pair. The product 0.691871 is the factor docs/evap-fvv.md 7.2 measures: omit it and the fixture lands 2.79 per cent high, uniformly within each fuel type. What breaks if this is wrong: nothing else in this calculator reads averageTankGasoline on a path that reaches MOVESOutput (0.3), so getting this wrong is the only way TankFuelGenerator can corrupt the answer -- and the only way it can be seen to matter.",
