        {
          "id": "the_two_fuel_types_bracket_different_rvp_knots",
          "description": "Fuel 1 at RVP 8.0 brackets knots 8 and 9; fuel 5 at RVP 7.7 brackets knots 7 and 8. The two adjustments differ in the third significant figure (0.691871 against 0.686534), and worked example C of docs/evap-fvv.md 6.3 is the only cell class in the fixture that separates them. What breaks if this is wrong: a port that interpolated both fuel types against one knot pair would be 0.8 per cent wrong on the 46 E85 cells and exactly right on the 82 gasoline ones, which is the shape of error a per-cell tolerance catches and a total does not.",
