        {
          "id": "tvv5_is_two_forms_and_eighteen_coefficient_rows",
          "description": "MOVES stores TVV-5's venting equations as VARCHAR in cumTVVCoeffs, and the execution database carries them already rewritten to eighteen labels T0..T5 and L0..L11 with no expression anywhere (docs/evap-fvv.md 2.10). Factored, they are TWO forms: a quadratic root and a convex blend of two of them, plus one linear leak term. This test evaluates the blend at a load where both roots are POSITIVE and differ (11.1396 and 2.8885, so the 0.8/0.2 weight is discriminating) and, in tvvEquationT3Clamped, at a load where both are negative, so max(0, .) is what returns the answer. T0 is asserted through the SAME template at weight 1, which is the claim that one expression covers all six labels. What breaks if this is wrong: nothing in MOVESOutput -- 0.3 measures that doubling this equation leaves all 128 cells bit-identical -- which is exactly why it has to be checked here.",
